---
description: Process a persistent-world player action through character-scoped legality, simulator effects and read-back state continuity.
args:{ sourceRecord: GameWorld; sourceEvidence: EvidenceItem[]; world:PersistentWorldState; utterance:PlayerUtterance; checkpoint:GameCheckpoint; receipts:WorldTransitionReceipt[]; readback?:WorldSimulatorReadback }
returns:GameSessionResult
---
Read `worldId`, `ruleSetId`, `sessionIds`, `directorId` and `contentBoundaryIds` from the top level of the GameWorld record. Never replace the authoritative IDs, rule version or content boundaries with generic fixture values. Bind actualReadback to readback when supplied, otherwise null. Bind resume = `reconcileGameCheckpoint(world, checkpoint, sourceRecord, sourceEvidence, actualReadback)`. If resume.ready is false, return a complete GameSessionResult with no intent, views, actions, receipts, belief changes or effects; preserve resume.checkpoint and set blocked with its exact blockers.

Bind intent = `interpretPlayerIntent(world, utterance, sourceRecord, sourceEvidence)`. Speech that claims an outcome does not execute it. If intent.questions is nonempty or intent.unresolved contains a consequential ambiguity, return a complete needs-clarification result with the questions and unchanged world/checkpoint; do not submit candidate actions.

Bind perspective = `projectCharacterKnowledge(world, utterance.characterId, intent.actions)`. Bind selection = `chooseLegalCharacterActions(world, utterance, perspective, intent.actions, sourceRecord, sourceEvidence)`. Return all rejected action findings in the result's continuityNotes; do not expose private facts. If no action remains eligible, return blocked with no simulator effect and preserve the current checkpoint.

Bind reconciliation = `applyWorldReceipts(world, selection.actions, receipts, resume.checkpoint, actualReadback)`. It accepts only exact action/revision receipts joined to the authoritative simulator readback. Bind continuity = `updateBeliefsAndContinuity(world, reconciliation, resume.checkpoint)`. Use its worldState and checkpoint for the result. Pending or unknown effects leave beliefs, state and replay cursor unchanged. Rejected simulator actions are actual outcomes but do not mutate the world.

Bind effectPreparation = `prepareWorldActionEffects(world, selection.actions, continuity.checkpoint, reconciliation)`. It prepares one `apply-player-actions` effect only for a new pending clientActionId, or `read-action-status` for an action already pending or unknown; never resend without an actual not-received readback. The returned checkpoint retains the idempotency key before any retry. Emit no effect for an acknowledged, rejected, clarified or blocked action. Effects are typed intentions; only returned receipt and readback can establish execution. Return a complete GameSessionResult with the original intent, questions, character perspective, selected legal actions, actual receipts, observed belief updates, continuity notes, the effectPreparation.checkpoint, actual readback world or unchanged input world, effectPreparation.effects and status derived from the reconciliation outcome.
